  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) Develop and validate ultrastructural membrane expansion microscopy (umExM): a method based on rationally designed membrane-anchorable probes and optimized expansion microscopy to densely label cellular membranes in fixed tissues, preserve ultrastructure, and enable nanoscale visualization and tracing of membranous structures, including higher-resolution iterative expansion imaging, using standard confocal microscopy.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) Combining membrane-compatible probe design with an optimized expansion microscopy workflow can address the need for dense membrane labeling while preserving ultrastructure and enabling nanoscale visualization with conventional optical readout."];
  "R6" [label="(0,0,0) Because achieving dense labeling in fixed tissues has remained challenging, and uniform and continuous membrane labeling would preserve ultrastructure alongside visualization of associated proteins, there is a need for a method that enables uniform membrane labeling in fixed tissues."];
